---

Deploy Appwrite on a DigitalOcean Droplet with the Appwrite Docker installer.

{% info title="Marketplace app" %}
The Appwrite 1-Click app is no longer available on the DigitalOcean Marketplace. Use the steps below to install Appwrite on a Droplet instead.
{% /info %}

# Install on a Droplet {% #install-on-droplet %}

{% section #create-droplet step=1 title="Create a Droplet" %}

1. In the [DigitalOcean Control Panel](https://cloud.digitalocean.com), create a Droplet.
2. Choose your configuration:
   - **Image**: The [Docker](https://marketplace.digitalocean.com/apps/docker) app from the Marketplace, which comes with Docker Engine and Docker Compose, or any Linux image you install Docker on yourself
   - **Size**: At least 2 CPU cores and 4GB of RAM, as listed in the [system requirements](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/installation#system-requirements)
   - **Region**: Select the region closest to your users
   - **SSH keys**: Add your SSH key for access
3. Click **Create Droplet**

{% /section %}

{% section #install-appwrite step=2 title="Run the installer" %}

1. If you use a DigitalOcean Cloud Firewall or a firewall on the Droplet, allow inbound traffic on ports 80 and 443, and on port 20080 while the setup wizard runs.
2. Connect to the Droplet over SSH.
3. Run the macOS and Linux [installation command](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/installation#installation-commands).

{% /section %}

{% section #complete-setup step=3 title="Complete setup" %}

1. Open `http://<DROPLET_IP>:20080` in a web browser.
2. Complete the [setup wizard](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/installation#setup-wizard) following the prompts.
3. Close port 20080 after the installation completes.

{% /section %}

# Custom installations {% #custom-installations %}

To configure the installation yourself instead of using the setup wizard, follow the [manual installation](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/installation#manual-installation) steps on the Droplet.

# Production considerations {% #production %}

For production deployments, optimization, and advanced configuration, see the [production deployment guide](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production).

# Next steps {% #next-steps %}

After successful deployment:

- [Configure services](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/configuration) - Set up email, storage, and other services
- [Production optimization](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production) - Prepare for production workloads
